{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794596059,"nonce":"v308DhBuN8VBb8hCa595JeGYZEE=","title":"ScalarView.integrate drops a positional argument, so expr.integrate(fem) fails on a bound field","message":"The documented FEM functional expr.integrate(fem) fails when expr is a bound scalar field: ScalarView.integrate(self, **kwargs) takes keywords only. Repro: ui = u.bind(x=x, y=y); fem = jno.fem([...]); ui.integrate(fem) and (1.0 * ui).integrate(fem) raise TypeError: ScalarView.integrate() takes 1 positional argument but 2 were given; ui._expr.integrate(fem) works and fem.eval(ui, sol) gives the value. Expected: the view forwards var (and the other arguments) to Placeholder.integrate.","files":null}]}